+## `bin/clean-workspaces.sh`
+
+Removes stale build workspaces: each direct subdirectory of the workspace root whose newest
+file is more than the age threshold old (an empty directory is aged by its own mtime).
+Symlinks in the root are never followed or removed.
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh [-n|--dry-run] [-r|--root DIR] [-d|--days N]
+```
+
+| Option | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `-r`, `--root DIR` | `workspaces` | Workspace root (relative to the current directory, or absolute) |
+| `-d`, `--days N` | `7` | Remove workspaces older than `N` days (non-negative integer) |
+| `-n`, `--dry-run` | off | List what would be removed (`would remove <dir> (age Nd)`) and remove nothing |
+| `-h`, `--help` | | Show usage |
+
+Examples:
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh --dry-run                       # preview with the defaults
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh --root /srv/ci/workspaces --days 14
+```
+
+Exit status: `0` on success, `1` if a removal failed, `64` for a usage error (bad option,
+non-numeric `--days`, or a root that resolves to `/`), `66` if the root is not a directory.
